WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
Now we will be treating
the orbicularis oculi.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.160
The upper portion of the orbicularis
oculi is a depressor muscle,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.160
while the lower aspect
is an elevator muscle.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.660
We will be injecting both
the upper and lower portion,

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.680
the upper to achieve a brow lift
and the lower to treat crow's feet.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.720
As you can see, the lower portion
of the orbicularis oculi pulls

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.200
up as the patient smiles.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.060
We will now be administering two
units per injection point for a

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.100
superficial depth.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.140
Two units per mark underneath
the brow arch and on the tail.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.000
And then also two units
on the crow's feet,

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.220
a little bit more superficially
here on the lower portion of those

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.220
crow's feet.
